sunxi: orangepi-zero: use conservative DRAM settings

Use 408 MHz DRAM configuration instead of the upstream 624 MHz
setting to favor memory stability on Orange Pi Zero.

This follows Armbian's board-specific configuration, not a locally
validated guarantee of stability on every board revision.

Armbian reference:
https://github.com/armbian/build/blob/main/patch/u-boot/u-boot-sunxi/board_orangepizero/adjust-default-dram-clockspeeds.patch

diff --git a/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig b/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero_defconfig
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="sun8i-h2-plus-orangepi-zero"
 CONFIG_SPL=y
 CONFIG_MACH_SUN8I_H3=y
-CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=624
+CONFIG_DRAM_CLK=408
 # CONFIG_VIDEO_DE2 is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_SPI_SUNXI=y
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
